A||N||25||Fiero5||Annual Super PFF member weekend get together||||6||
Z||000000||Fiero5||08-20-2001||10:05 AM||||Read this carefully and let me know what you think of this idea. You too Cliff, as PFF is your baby after all.<P>I was thinking that we could start a HUGE annual PFF member get together. We could have two of them, one on each side of the country on the same day. That way we could share what was happening via the internet/PFF/live video cams at both spots at the same time sort of thing. Something similar to those who posted updates during Carlisle this year.<P>This could be like Wrestlmania, the Olympics or the Superbowl of Fiero events that everyone could look forward to each year. People would plan their vacations around the places chosen for the host sites each year. We could then create two next years calendars, one showing one site and one from the other site and those who attended. Of course I am sure everyone would want to buy one of each. Special shirts, one unique to each site could be created, window graphics made showing which PFF show site you attended that year, similar to what the Hot Rod Power Tour does. We could also get big sponsors offering prizes, advertising in the various club newsletters of their area that dwarf anything ever seen at a Fiero event to date.<P>One of the days could even be a show with huge unique trophies, a huge cookout and Fiero events all rolled into one HUGE weekend. Clubs from all over the country would come together as one for the Annual PFF Weekend Super Event. PFF members from around the world could come to either site, as all Fiero lovers merge into a melting pot of one huge Fiero event like nothing ever seen before.<P>Even a huge cruise could be set up. With some calls made to local TV stations (I bet if given enough advance notice, even CNN would cover it) with a chance of a news story done on such a huge annual event around one car, the Pontiac Fiero. Even PFF members could shoot video footage, to edit later into a video for purchase showing hundreds of PFF members and their awesome rides like nothing that has ever been seen. <BR>Then, some of the procedes from the selling of merchaindise could go into an annual PFF fund for needy children or something, so we can help out those in need while having a great time. We could turn this into a realy unique chance to step up a level above what any other car club, car BB or anyone else has ever done. We could be the first to do anything even remotely like this.<P>I am serious with this idea.  This will only happen though if we all get coordinated and actually work together to make it happen.<BR>What does everyone think?<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pegasuscolors_sig_copy.jpg">    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||10:14 AM||||I'm certainly not opposed to something like that... would be a lot of fun!  Small problem- from here in Minn, neither the East coast or West coast is close (That's why I didn't go out to the FOCOA nat'ls).  If you keep it off the coast, then most people will be traveling more equal distances.  I've been to 4 FOCOA nationals- 2 at Pontiac Michigan, and 2 at Indy.  Both distances are reasonable for travel... <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig2.jpg">    <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||08-20-2001||10:28 AM||||One of the first things that would have to be ironed out is the location(s). Unfortunately, it will be more convenient for some than others as we all have experienced with any show/get together that we travel to. That is why I thought up the dual sites. So those on the East coast don't have to travel all the way to the West coast, and vice versa. The nice thing is we can choose different host sites each year, so if it is not a close location(s) or convenient date(s) for some one year, the following year may be better for some.<P>I remember reading about the now famous first Star Trek convention that was held in New York many, many years ago. They expected a few hundred people, and literally thousands showed up. Let's not sell our Fiero community short. This could be BIG!<BR>To semi quote a famous saying: "If you build it, they will come".<P>Steve||||reg||7
Z||000003||Cheever3000||08-20-2001||10:36 AM||||I'll have to make you an official Texan, cause you think <B>BIG</B>, mister!  I like it!  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-20-2001||11:54 AM||||That would be awesome!  Great idea!||||reg||6
Z||000005||Songman||08-20-2001||12:03 PM||||I may be a little biased but Nashville can be reached easier from the most places of any city in the US. I forget where that info came from, but that is why Nashville is such a big shipping hub... <P>Let's do it here!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000006||Elvira||08-20-2001||01:16 PM||||How about dividing the country into 4 sections and picking 4 central areas that way.  Might make it a little easier for people to be able go.  Same concept, but four locations instead of just the two.  I'm sure alot of people would be more inclined to go if the only had about 500 miles to drive.  Definately a cool idea Steve! <P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero5||08-20-2001||02:12 PM||||4 sites would work OK I guess, as long as the coordination worked for all 4 sites. Probably would want to select a "leader(s)" for each site to help coordinate it for that area. Each sites graphics/poster/T-shirt design would have the same PFF logo/theme to keep them all tied together to the main idea, but then each site could add a little something extra to make it unique for that site also.<P>I guess doing it this way, it would be sorta like the various Planet Hollywood sites, with the graphics all being the same. You have one that says Planet Hollywood New York, one that says Planet Hollywood Florida, etc. That kind of thing. We could do "PFF New York 2002" on the front and then the unique graphics for that site on the back. If it was in New York, you could have the statue of Liberty with a few different Fiero styles within that graphic design. Be kinda cool.<P>Steve<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000008||XDrewX||08-20-2001||02:27 PM||||This sounds great !!!<P>I had a question along these lines:<P>Will there be another Fiero event @ Carlisle PA in 2002.  I missed 2001.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierobear||08-20-2001||03:27 PM||||Maybe just do it at each year's national show? Next year is in Missouri, which shouldn't be too bad for most people east of the Rockies. My wife and I might make the drive from California.<P>As for the west coast, our Western Regional wouldn't be a bad place to do it. Next year is in Lake Tahoe (fairly central to the west coast), and 2003 will be a combined show with the national show in Las Vegas.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ditz88GT||08-20-2001||04:10 PM||||I have an idea! (Wow that doesn't happen a lot)  Why don't we take a map and figure out where the most Fiero owners are and figure out locations from that.  Like if say Daytona is filled with PFF members and there is two in Boston, it would make more sense to have it down south somewhere rather than Boston.  Maybe we could look at the general areas with the most Fiero people and go from there.  I live in Lancaster PA, so I feel we should have it here...but that wouldn't really be fair if 50 Fiero owners live in Maine.  Just some Ideas, what do you think?<P><P>------------------<BR>~Ditz88GT<P>E-mail: cditzler@hotmail.com<BR>AIM: Ditz88GT<BR>http://go.to/fiero||||reg||1
