Z||000013||Cheever3000||08-20-2001||05:21 PM||||Several good ideas in the posts above.  But after dreaming of all the Fiero events to attend this year, I was lucky to make <B>one</B> (a small one).  I do want to attend the FOCOA Missouri event next year, but doubt if I could <B>also</B> make it to a separate PFF meeting far away.  <P>So, I'm agreeing with the proposal of having this in conjunction with the National meet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||dlancer407||08-20-2001||05:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85ZainoGT:<BR><B>ok, so, Indianapolis is the crossroads of america if you see where im going   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  got the raceway museum and everything out here...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My brother and I went to a couple of Shelby Dodge nationals at Indy since 1995.They had a car show under the grandstand and we got to drive our cars on the race track.It was the most fun I have ever had at a car show<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jaygee79||08-20-2001||06:07 PM||||I think it's a good idea.  I personally think there should be one in New England.  There are a lot of Fiero people around here.  NEFA, MAFOA, FOCONE, they all are in this general area.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
