Z||000017||Fiero5||08-20-2001||09:44 PM||||I had allready given thought to combining something like this with another show. But if you think about it, we basically do that allready at any Fiero event, be it a regular car show or Fiero only. Any show we go to we see some people that are Pennocks folks. Last fall at the FOCONE Fall show in Rutland Mass, Phil Randolph had a Pennocks sign posted up on his Supercharged Formulas antenna. There were many Pennocks members there including myself & Fiero2, Chester & Elvira, Phil, Cobra, Boomtastic, etc.<P>I thought it would be alot more fun to have this special, all by itself. Especially with the multiple sites idea so those who can't make a big show somewhere one year might be able to make one of these.<BR>Also, the nationals is put on by FOCOA isn't it? I think having a second big event by a seperate groupe would be a great idea.<BR>I would say that allthough I agree PA is a great site for a Fiero show, they allready have two each year. Fieros at Carlisle and the Fiero Dutch Classic. For many of us in New England anyway, PA is literally an all day drive requiring two nights stay over at least, food for all that time and all that. If we had multiple sites, then we could have one site say in New York. This would then be alot closer for many of us New Englander folks than say PA, Alabama, West Virginia or Florida. Then other sites can be carefully chosen also that allow those who are normally looking at a full days drive or more in other areas of the country, a better chance to make a big event without having to rearange half their year in advance to be able to try and go. I don't think we would take anything away from any of the other shows, as I know if I still had the ability to go to one of those also, I would. I think there is plenty of room for growth, especially with more shows.<P>As I notice more and more Fiero people coming on line, getting on Pennocks and joining clubs, it would seem to make sense that we could use another large Fiero event. We can't all make every show every year that is within a days drive of where we live. I know many Fiero owners who try to go to as many shows as they can. Others pick and choose and get their fill on just a few each year. Either way, this is a great opportunity to build on what is allready growing by leaps and bounds each year. The many Fiero owners old and new who love this great piece of American automotive history. Americas first and only mid engine two seat sports car.<P>Having said that however, it is ultimately what we all as Pennocks members decide what works best. If we all decide that maybe combining it to an allready existing  show works bette, than we can do that. Whatever works the best to get this off the ground. Right?<P>Just some thoughts.<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000018||Cheever3000||08-20-2001||09:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I thought it would be alot more fun to have this special, all by itself. Especially with the multiple sites idea so those who can't make a big show somewhere one year might be able to make one of these... ...Whatever works the best to get this off the ground. Right?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>All true.  You're right.  But although some things can be decided by majority, other things you'll just have to say "This is how it's going to be".  And we'll adjust.  It's your baby, so you tell us.  But I definitely like where you're going with this.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||hugh||08-20-2001||10:08 PM||||What about our Canadian members?||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fiero5||08-20-2001||10:35 PM||||I have been racking my brain on that very thought the last day or so when I came up with this idea. Figuring in Canada makes it interesting. Canada covers as much distance mileage wise as the whole US. Actually, it stretches further than figuring from Maine to California if I am not mistaken. When you consider the Fiero members on each end of Canada and in the middle, and the driving time to reach any point in the US that is some serious driving time! If we say, OK, let's have a Canadian site also, that isn't so simple either. Anywhere we place one site in Canada, it can be hundreds and hundreds of miles for others in the same section of the country alone. And what about AusFiero or our European Fiero brothers and sisters. Ausfiero could coordinate a site there. We could maybe have a site in England, one in Hungary, etc.<P>Now some of you can see even a small piece of what I meant about this having the possiblity of being really big. Simultaneous Annual PFF Events all over the world. Just look at a big picture of that for a moment and really think about it. Picture it being sort of like what they do with simultaneous New Year Eve celebrations all over the world.<P>Kinda cool, huh?<P>To answer your question, I guess hearing from a few of our Canadian Fiero members from either end and a few in the middle would help  in begining to figure that part of it out.<P>Steve||||reg||10
Z||000021||Jaygee79||08-20-2001||10:45 PM||||World-wide wouldn't be so easy though.  When it's daytime here it's the middle of the night in other countries.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Fiero5||08-20-2001||10:58 PM||||That's true, but if we turned it into a big weekend event, then when we are winding down at the end of one day, those in other parts of the world would just be gearing up. Just think about us here the next morning jumping on a computer to see what transpired at the over seas sites that night.<P>Also, being over a two day weekend would allow some to come one day that wouldn't be able to make the other due to work, family, distance or whatever.<P>Again this has been an idea presented up for all to see in just the past day, so it is going to be tweeked and played with and tweeked some more I'm sure.<P>It can also start off kinda small at first, and grow over a period of time. We don't need to start off the very first one with a bang at full size. Though with so many enthusiastic Pennocks members allready spread out all over, and continuing to grow more and more, it would be quite easy to have this start right out with a bang from the start.<P>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000023||maryjane||08-21-2001||02:43 AM||||I'd like to see it rotate from one area of the country to another year to year. It's over 200 miles in any direction JUST to the state line from where I live, those in San Antonio area, even further. Two day event sounds good. Keep us posted.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Fierochic88||08-21-2001||03:37 PM||||Definitely could be fun....<P>Jennifer||||reg||1
